SOC Leads, Threat Intelligence, IR On-call,

JOINT THREAT HUNT - RVV-2026-9002 ("Water Curupira").
Your organization's sector is in the active targeting
scope of a financially motivated intrusion set tracked
as Water Curupira. Initial-access brokers associated
with the set have re-used credentials matching
patterns seen in your sector. You are invited to
join a time-boxed joint hunt (JCDC-coordinated)
starting Monday.

1. CAMPAIGN SUMMARY (TLP:CLEAR PORTION)

  Tracking ID:      RVV-2026-9002
  Intrusion set:    Water Curupira (financially
                    motivated, IAB activity)
  Sectors in scope: Industrial automation,
                    precision manufacturing,
                    logistics
  Observed TTPs:    TA0001 (T1190, T1133),
                    TA0006 (T1110.004),
                    TA0004 (T1486)
  IOCs shared
    to date:        214 (72 domains, 96 IPs,
                    46 hashes)
  Relevance
    to your org:    One harvested-credential dump
                    references a domain pattern
                    matching your legacy SSO
                    portal

2. HOW PRIVATE-SECTOR PARTICIPATION ACTUALLY WORKS

  CISA will NEVER:
  - Email an onboarding kit, connection profile,
    .mobileconfig, .ovpn, or any executable /
    configuration attachment to prospective
    participants
  - Ask you to install software or profiles from
    an email in order to "join a hunt" or "join
    JCDC"
  - Operate recruitment through lookalike
    domains such as "cisa-jtt" or
    "jcdc-partners" relay addresses
  - Set an "activate before the weekend"
    deadline for telemetry admission

  Actual participation path:
  1. Type the JCDC page address yourself:
     cisa.gov.example/jcdc (do not use links
     from email).
  2. Submit the sector-participation request
     signed by your designated point of contact.
  3. Telemetry sharing, if you choose it, is
     configured BY YOUR TEAM using published
     STIX-TAXII / AIS API documentation, on
     infrastructure you control, after your own
     change review.
  4. IOC feeds flow through the same official
     AIS channels you already use.

3. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Search the advisory ID RVV-2026-9002 in the
    public catalog (typed URL) before acting
  - Cross-check with your sector ISAC
  - Report lookalike recruitment emails to
    report.cisa.gov.example (typed) and to your
    internal security team

4. ABOUT THE "INCIDENT CORRELATION" CLAIM

  References to your internal incident numbers
  (e.g., "INC-2026-0417 possibly related") in an
  unsolicited email are a known pressure tactic:
  verify any such claim inside your own incident
  tracker, not by replying to the message.

